Round venus's host-visible allocations up to the guest's page size.

A host-visible VkDeviceMemory reaches the guest as a virtio-gpu blob: venus
asks the host driver for the memory, the renderer exports it as a dma-buf, and
the guest kernel creates a blob over it. The kernel rounds a blob's size up to
its own pages; the renderer then refuses any blob larger than the dma-buf it
was given:

    vkr: mem dma_buf_size 4096 < blob_size 16384
    virgl_cmd_resource_create_blob: virgl blob create error: Invalid argument

An aarch64 Tessera kernel uses 16K pages and an x86_64 Linux host 4K ones, so
every small mappable allocation fails, and the first thing to fail in the guest
is whatever needed it -- Ember's frame synchronisation objects, reported as
"could not create frame synchronization objects". An Apple-silicon host has 16K
pages too and never sees it.

Rounding the allocation up in the guest makes the host's dma-buf as large as the
blob. Imports are left alone: their size is the imported object's.

--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_device_memory.c
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@
 
 #include "vn_device_memory.h"
 
+#include "util/os_misc.h"
+
 #include "venus-protocol/vn_protocol_driver_device_memory.h"
 #include "venus-protocol/vn_protocol_driver_transport.h"
 
@@ -373,6 +375,30 @@
       }
    }
 
+   /* Tessera: a blob is made of the guest's pages, so the kernel rounds its
+    * size up to them, and the renderer refuses a blob larger than the memory
+    * the host driver exported for it. A guest whose pages are larger than the
+    * host's -- 16K on aarch64 over a 4K host -- asks for 4096 bytes, gets a
+    * 4096-byte dma-buf from the host and a 16384-byte blob from its kernel,
+    * and the blob is refused with nothing in the guest saying why. Rounding a
+    * host-visible allocation up to the guest's page size makes the two agree;
+    * the extra bytes are never handed to the caller as anything but slack. */
+   VkMemoryAllocateInfo page_aligned_info;
+   if (!import_fd_info) {
+      const VkMemoryType *mem_type =
+         &dev->physical_device->memory_properties
+             .memoryTypes[pAllocateInfo->memoryTypeIndex];
+      uint64_t page_size = 4096;
+      os_get_page_size(&page_size);
+      if ((mem_type->propertyFlags & VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT) &&
+          pAllocateInfo->allocationSize % page_size) {
+         page_aligned_info = *pAllocateInfo;
+         page_aligned_info.allocationSize =
+            align64(pAllocateInfo->allocationSize, page_size);
+         pAllocateInfo = &page_aligned_info;
+      }
+   }
+
    struct vn_device_memory *mem = vk_device_memory_create(
       &dev->base.base, pAllocateInfo, pAllocator, sizeof(*mem));
    if (!mem)
